	(text "Half-wave rectifier, bulk capacitor, supply monitor"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 123.19 38.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0c98f81d-4aa2-5326-b7d4-674f23d804a1")
	)
	(text "U1       LM5164, 100 V synchronous buck (TI SNVSAU4D). It survives the 77.4 V clamp level.\n         V_BUCK = 1.2 V x (1 + (R3 + R4) / R5) = 5.28 V, 5.16 to 5.40 V over tolerance.\nR2       47k sets the on-time: 281 kHz.\nF5, D25  For a switch of U1 that fails short (section 4.8). D25, SMBJ6.0A, holds V_BUCK under\n         10 V and F5, 0.5 A very fast, opens. F5 is soldered: it opens only when U1 has failed.\n         Do not fit a larger rating. Its 0.42 ohm also limits the fault current.\nC4       2.2 nF bootstrap. The datasheet fixes this value; a larger one damages the part.\nR6, C7, C8   Type 3 ripple injection: 24 mV at FB at 34 V in, 13 mV at 10 V.\nL1       47 uH, Isat 2.0 A. Ripple 0.34 A, peak 0.99 A against a 1.25 A current limit.\nLoad on V_BUCK: 0.28 A typical, 0.78 A peak (section 4.2). It also feeds the relay coil and\nthe sensor supply directly, and V5 through D3 on the USB sheet.\n\nLAYOUT: C2 and C3 at U1 pins 2 and 1 with the shortest loop, behind F5. Keep the SW node small and away\nfrom the current-sense parts. PWR_FLAG marks nets that are fed through a passive part."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 226.06 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0fd258d6-96e7-5e06-a5ba-523057d4cf1c")
	)
	(text "Input fuse, LM5164 buck converter, 5.28 V, over-voltage clamp"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 205.74 38.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "171f8b4f-adac-5fef-aa73-154c0e84d58d")
	)
	(text "24 VAC INPUT AND LOGIC SUPPLY (hardware design section 4).\n\nF4, F1   3 A time-lag fuses in holders, one in each transformer leg (section 5.3 says why two).\n         Terminal 2, AC_N, becomes circuit GND behind F1. Both holders sit in the fuse well behind J1.\nD1       SMCJ48CA: stands off 48 V, above the 45.3 V peak of 32 VAC. Clamps at 77.4 V.\nD2, R1   Half-wave rectifier. R1 is the surge-rated SR2512JK (5 %), not the FK (1 %) part:\n         it takes 237 to 385 W for about 1 ms when the board is plugged in at the mains peak.\nC1       470 uF 63 V, through-hole, on the bottom side lying down. VIN_DC is 26 to 31 V at 24 VAC\n         and 44 V at 32 VAC with no load. Ripple 0.16 A typical, 0.48 A at the peak corner.\nR9, R10  VIN_MON = VIN_DC / 31 to GPIO3: about 0.97 V at 24 VAC, 1.43 V at 32 VAC.\nR7, R8   Under-voltage lockout of U1: on at 9.0 V, off at 8.4 V. On VIN_DC, before F5."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "36fd7feb-56ff-5a51-abae-dc9402d6ee6e")
	)
	(text "24 VAC input: a fuse in each leg, surge clamp"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.67 38.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ccf01537-3967-5950-ba96-58b122fe1e6a")
	)
